 "ufgSpecifics": "Regulation: Resolução CONSUNI 39/2020 ('Regulamento das Ações de Extensão e Cultura', revoked CONSUNI 03/2008), still the base rule after the 2026 renaming of PROEC to PROEX (CONSUNI 355/2026); culture now sits with SEACULT, but the regulation and system still use the expression 'ação de extensão e/ou cultura'. Five modalidades: programa, projeto, curso, evento, prestação de serviço. Programa = at least 3 projects with different coordinators, optionally with courses, events and services, 3-10 years. Projeto = 1-5 years, may be linked to a programa (the SIGAA form asks 'vinculada a um Programa de Extensão?', and the link can be added after approval). Registration: every action must be registered by its coordinator in the SIGAA Módulo Extensão in the year it runs and may start only after PROEX validation. Coordination: the coordinator must be an active UFG servidor in exercise (docente or técnico-administrativo em educação); the vice-coordinator may be external; the team must include at least one student (discente) and a vice-coordinator (manual 2025); every member must take part in at least one activity. The 'unidade proponente' must be the coordinator's lotação, and other units may be added as co-executoras. Roles by bond: docente (avaliador, colaborador, consultor, coordenador, palestrante, vice-coordenador); TAE (avaliador, colaborador, consultor, coordenador, participante, vice-coordenador); discente (avaliador, bolsista, integrante de equipe, voluntário); externo (avaliador, colaborador, consultor, ministrante, outros, palestrante, vice-coordenador, voluntário). ACEx coordinated by a TAE must include docente(s) supervising the students (CEPEC 1699/2021 art. 20). Governance: each unidade acadêmica must have a CAEX (Coordenação das Atividades de Extensão e Cultura), with at least two effective servidores (presidente and suplente), appointed by the Conselho Diretor; UAEs and órgãos may create one (one per unit). If there is no CAEX, the unit's direction takes over. Câmpus Goiás has a Coordenação de Extensão e Cultura above its CAEX. The Câmara Superior de Extensão e Cultura (CEPEC) settles omitted cases, and PROEX has a Câmara de Extensão e Cultura (CEC). Who may propose (CEPEC 1699/2021 art. 9): any Unidade Acadêmica, Unidade Acadêmica Especial, CEPAE, Pró-Reitorias and órgãos. Curricularização: ACEx at least 10% of total course workload (CNE/CES 7/2018; CEPEC 1699/2021). Students only earn ACEx as team members, never as audience; monitorias and tutorias aimed at the internal community do not count. Reports: an annual partial report or a final report is required, evaluated by CAEX, approved by the unit direction and validated by PROEX. If a report is not submitted within 60 days after each year, the coordinator is blocked from registering new actions or joining new teams. Scholarship students must also submit reports. Certificates are released only after the partial or final report. A finished action can be duplicated for a new period once PROEX has validated its final report. Unfunded actions cannot be extended: they must be closed and duplicated. After approval only the team, objectives and activities, financing, programa link and ACEx curriculum link can be edited; the period cannot. Fees: courses and events that charge fees must reserve at least 10% of places free of charge for people in financial vulnerability. Financing comes through PROBEC (Programa de Bolsas de Extensão e Cultura) calls or external funds via a Fundação de Apoio or UFG agreement (Resolução CONSUNI 42/2020). Events are managed and certified through the Plateia UFG platform, only for actions in status 'Em Execução'. Public data is available on SIGAA Public and Analisa UFG (analisa.ufg.br/p/32231-extensao).",
